{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block h1 %}<h1>Privacy notice.</h1>{% endblock %}
{% block lead %}How {{ cfg.legal_name }} handles the data you send through this site.{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
  <!-- [[TODO before launch: a data protection lawyer reviews this notice (PRD-W section 8.3)]] -->
  <section class="ex-section">
    <div class="ex-wrap">
      <h2>Who is responsible.</h2>
      <p class="ex-measure">{{ cfg.legal_name }} is the controller. Its registered address is [[TODO registered address in India]]. Contact: <a href="mailto:{{ cfg.contact_email }}">{{ cfg.contact_email }}</a>.</p>
      <h2>What we collect.</h2>
      <p class="ex-measure">The details you send us by email, and server logs. The logs keep a truncated IP address and no more.</p>
      <h2>Why, and on what basis.</h2>
      <p class="ex-measure">To reply to your enquiry and to take steps before a contract (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)). To keep the site secure (Art. 6(1)(f)).</p>
      <h2>Who receives it.</h2>
      <p class="ex-measure">Our hosting provider and our email provider. Each acts under a data processing agreement.</p>
      <h2>Transfers outside the EU.</h2>
      <p class="ex-measure">Our team reads enquiries in India. India has no EU adequacy decision. The basis is your own request before a contract (Art. 49(1)(b)), and standard contractual clauses with our processors.</p>
      <h2>How long we keep it.</h2>
      <p class="ex-measure">Enquiries: 6 months, unless they lead to a contract. Server logs: 14 days.</p>
      <h2>Your rights.</h2>
      <p class="ex-measure">You may ask for access, correction, erasure, restriction, objection and portability. You may complain to a data protection authority.</p>
      <h2>Cookies, tracking and automated decisions.</h2>
      <p class="ex-measure">This site sets no cookies and uses no tracking. We make no automated decisions about you.</p>
      <h2>India.</h2>
      <p class="ex-measure">The main duties of India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act apply from 13 May 2027. We write this notice so that it also meets them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
{% endblock %}
